A||||20||FieroPerformance||3 reasons I am glad they stopped making fieros...||||6||
Z||000000||FieroPerformance||10-27-2001||12:27 AM||||Before you get mad understand that I love Fieros and have nothing against them, but the other day I realized part of the reason I like them so much is because they aren't in production anymore...<P>1. They are rare, but not too rare. They are rare enough to turn heads but not too rare to find parts when needed.<P>2. Due to the short lifespan, most of the parts are interchangable and most FAQs and techical problems apply to all models. This really helps out on the forum when people have questions.<P>3. If they would have continued to make them our cars would look very out of date compared to the new models.<P>You may agree with me, you may not. I just thought I would share my thoughts    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>-Charlie<P>edited becase it is 12:30 in the morning and I said they were made for 4 years. I feel very stupid right now. Goodnight.<BR>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpic.jpg">   <P>[This message has been edited by FieroPerformance (edited 10-27-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by FieroPerformance (edited 10-27-2001).]||||reg||6
Z||000001||tgowens||10-27-2001||12:39 AM||||I agree with 1, 3, and part of 2. They were actually made for 5 years ('84, '85, '86, '87 and '88) and for the most part, parts are interchangeable with certain exceptions on the '88.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Pontiaddict||10-27-2001||12:49 AM||||If you want to get technical, they made Fieros from 1983-1988.||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroPerformance||10-27-2001||12:52 AM||||You guys are killing me. I am taking out that ().||||reg||1
