Z||000018||KathyHL||10-28-2001||09:50 AM||||I have to agree with you on all the points you made, FieroPerformance. It just makes the little car that more Special. Now, I wonder how badly they are going to insult the Camaro when the bring it back into production in a couple or few years. Front wheel drive? Probablhy a Geo. Look what they did to the Nova and Lemans, LOL!||||reg||1
Z||000019||Back On Holiday||10-28-2001||04:10 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by KathyHL:<BR><B>I have to agree with you on all the points you made, FieroPerformance. It just makes the little car that more Special. Now, I wonder how badly they are going to insult the Camaro when the bring it back into production in a couple or few years. Front wheel drive? Probablhy a Geo. Look what they did to the Nova and Lemans, LOL!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Every time I see one of the NEWER Model Novas that look like GEO METROS or Ford Aspires, I laugh...  Because GM ruined the rep of a nice muscle car by throwing in a rubber band engine.<P>I know, its not nice to laugh...but I can't help it.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000020||Fierozilla||10-28-2001||07:09 PM||||I agree. Those reasons do make the Fiero that much more special. I still love the looks and (good) comments I get from people.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>But you're right, GM would've DEFINANTLY screwed it up by now though. They're so concerned w/ the Corvette (very nice), trucks and SUV's, that the Fiero would've turned into some kind of joke Im sure.<BR>As far as the Mustangs go, 64 1/2 - 73 Mustangs were sweet. In 74 they went to the Mustang II which was garbage. In the 80s they were thugly! 1994 till now, they look sweet!||||reg||1
